 "title": "About Hear Plugin",
 "story": [
  {
   "type": "markdown",
   "id": "ba9751a5511afdbf",
   "text": "The **Hear** plugin walks a page-level GMap as a street and lets its pages speak: positional audio under a versioned soundscape policy, a deadband and an equal-power crossfade so voices do not flicker, a consent gate before anything sounds, and a transcript and provenance card for every voice. Built by Phase 3 of the Hear Crowds Plan on atlas.anarchive.earth."
  },
  {
   "type": "hear",
   "id": "36944e2bc3d2768e",
   "text": "MAP https://atlas.anarchive.earth/assets/hear-crowds-demo/map.json\nMEDIA https://atlas.anarchive.earth/assets/hear-crowds-demo/street-media.json\nPOLICY https://atlas.anarchive.earth/assets/hear-crowds-demo/soundscape-policy.json\nSTREET clause.legalcommons.org/right-to-amparo\nHEIGHT 520\nRight to Amparo and its sixteen houses, speaking."
  },
  {
   "type": "markdown",
   "id": "a7e1b8e9d6e34ef6",
   "text": "# Commands\n\nOne per line, UPPERCASE first word. Anything else is the caption."
  },
  {
   "type": "markdown",
   "id": "cd4c1040c3c51e52",
   "text": "- `MAP url` \u2014 the map.json a page-level GMap writes: positions, regions, edges, the street\n- `MEDIA url` \u2014 the street-media.json index: which houses speak and where their clips and manifests are\n- `POLICY url` \u2014 the soundscape-policy.json: emitter budget, intelligible limit, ducking, crossfade, deadband, dwell, weights\n- `STREET site/slug` \u2014 the square; defaults to the map's own street\n- `HEIGHT px` \u2014 the height of the place, 240 or more"
  },
  {
   "type": "markdown",
   "id": "73838ab426fb0a98",
   "text": "# How it sounds\n\nNothing plays before Enter the soundscape. Then a listener rides the camera and only the policy's budget of houses emit, ranked by proximity, focus and view direction. A house outside the intelligible limit murmurs through a low-pass filter. A challenger must beat the weakest voice by the deadband, and that voice must have dwelt at least the minimum before it gives way; every change is an equal-power crossfade. Click a house to stand at its threshold and read along; go inside for the page, its audio and its provenance; open the source page in the wiki from either. Without WebGL the street is a list of houses with players.\n\n# Controls\n\nDrag to look; W A S D walk, Q E up and down, or hold the arrow pad; F or the Full screen button fills the display, Esc leaves; Mute silences every bus, Pause voices stops the clips and keeps the place; Listening trial runs the One Audible Street questions."
  },
  {
